WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.250
When I came out of war captivity,

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:05.000
my friends,

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:06.250
especially the younger ones,

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:09.500
were unable to attend dance school.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:14.000
I then practised dancing with them at our home.

00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:28.250
I think this project

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:31.000
brought the whole class
together very closely.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:32.750
Yes, then you liked me again,

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:33.750
not before.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.750
We couldn't stand each other there.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.500
My heart just opens up

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:41.000
when I see what all this inspires in people.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.250
My wife used to say to me:

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:45.000
“Don't shake your shoulders.”

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:49.500
Yes, of course we danced the waltz,

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.500
especially the Viennese waltz, turning left.

00:00:52.250 --> 00:00:54.500
When you introduced the project to us,

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.000
it reminded me of the good feeling of my childhood,

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.250
and every memory from growing up came back to me.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.000
The youngest person in our project was nine years old

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.750
and the oldest was 96.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:11.500
I first went onto the dance floor when I was 15

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.250
and I never left.

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:20.000
Many of them couldn't remember their last dance.

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:22.500
But because of the project,

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.500
we could bring their memories
back to life.
